<http://data.silknow.org/object/01e1f7a2-6f52-33d2-a728-f1c9c7ad2742/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Tapestry panel woven in wool and silk in three shades of pink, six shades of green, three shades of brown, cream and maroon. The warp is of 3-ply white cotton, 26 threads to the inch.\n\nIt depicts, on a pale green ground a slender stem bears three clusters of five-petalled flowers and offshoots with long, slim leaves, filling a rectangle marked by a bead and reel moulding. Outside this is a plain maroon border."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/01e1f7a2-6f52-33d2-a728-f1c9c7ad2742> .

